# There is almost nothing here any more, and that is deliberate.
#
# The proxy system, the map upstreams, the response cache and the model — base
# URL, API key and model name — used to be about forty environment variables.
# They are now constants in the source:
#
#   src/lib/proxy-pool.ts     the dials: timeouts, attempts, budgets, how many
#                             working exits to keep, how hard to scrape
#   src/lib/proxy-sources.ts  which GitHub proxy lists to fetch
#   src/lib/osm-forward.ts    the upstreams and how long replies are cached
#   src/lib/endpoints.ts      where the BROWSER asks for the map
#   src/lib/ai.ts             the model gateway, its key and its model name
#
# Two reasons, both of them things that have actually gone wrong on this box:
#
#   * This app is built once and deployed to TWO machines. A setting that lives
#     in a per-machine file is a setting the two boxes can disagree about, and
#     "why is the other server behaving differently" is then a question with no
#     answer in the repository.
#   * pm2 stores an app's environment in dump.pm2 and replays it on restart,
#     resurrect and boot, and dotenv will not override a variable that is
#     already set. So an edited .env and a restarted app can disagree
#     indefinitely, with the file in front of you saying one thing and the
#     process doing another — `pm2 restart --update-env` does not fix it. It
#     has bitten this deployment three times, once on OSM_PROXY_ENTRY.
#     A constant in the source cannot go stale in a pm2 dump.
#
# Anything above that you want to change is a one-line edit and a rebuild, which
# is the panel's Update button.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The one setting left: where the crime reports are kept
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unset, the reports people file live in that browser's localStorage and are
# visible to nobody else. Set, they are rows in the `maddie` database and every
# visitor sees the same map. Which backend is in use is printed in the panel.
#
# On this deployment it must name BOTH replica-set members and the set, or each
# box quietly writes to its own copy — a failure that looks exactly like a
# working site until you fail over. Never drop the database name: without it
# the driver picks `test` and the app serves an empty map.
#
# MONGO_URI=mongodb://parsa.rs:27017,aschkan.rs:27017/maddie?replicaSet=rs0
